Thank you very much for your answers Prof. Håvard.

For future references, I would like to add that, in my specific case, changing the parameters of the "control.inla" function in the following way:

control.inla(strategy = "adaptive",
                      int.strategy = "eb")

improved SIGNIFICANTLY the performances of the model. I am now able to run it on my iMac (8 cores with 32 Gb each) in almost 8 minutes.

Best,

Nico

