Another obvious problem is that my individual SPDEs may be flawed and will transmit their problems to the model obtained by combination of the two basic SPDEs. However, I tested various simpler cases, all of which ran smoothly:
nonstationary Matérn latent field  +  "vanilla" homoscedastic Gaussian noise (specified via the "family" argument)
no spatially coherent latent field   +   heteroscedastic Gaussian noise (with control.family)
stationery Matérn latent field         +  heteroscedastic Gaussian noise (with control.family)
